Subject: [PATCH 4/4] C14, patch 4 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M20): THREE
 GENERATED VIEWS THAT QUOTE THE RECORD'S OWN LINES ARE WORKING INDICES,
 LABELLED SO WHERE THE README POINTS TO THEM

Main's M20 takes the verdict ledger and the spine off the public face as labelled working indices, because
they quote verdict lines word for word. Three more generated views are of the same kind, measured before this
patch: the context recovery (34 inner words), the closed doors (27) and the reviewer's view (9). Their inner
words are in the lines they quote (register rows, kill records, verdict lines, log entries), not in their
generator's text: the generator's own phrases with an inner word are its comments, and the heading of the
register rows that wait for the owner on the context recovery, which is main's own first read after a
compaction.

So, by the same reason as main's: the three are working indices, listed with the two in the gate and not
read by it; the README labels the context recovery and the closed doors as working indices where it points
to them (it does not point to the reviewer's view); and the gate's test holds that every working index the
README names is labelled near its mention. Their quotations are not rewritten.

THE BUILDER'S READING, and main's to change: whether a view a newcomer is sent to may be a labelled working
index, or must be rewritten by its generator. If the second, the context recovery's heading and the closed
doors' rows are where a generator would change.

The gate reads 14 pages now, 4 at zero, 1,387 words. Not checked by main.
